84704 #edb/ref 1071 "Let ${D}_{i}=\\{2i-1,-i,1,i+2\\},$ where $i\\in \\{0,2,3,5\\}.$ Then, ${D}_{0}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284704 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2c511297-a581-5325-971e-3c832a3d5acf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284704 #edb/ref 1074 "To write down the elements of ${D}_{0},$ we substitute $i=0$ into the expression and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{0} & =\\{2(0)-1,-0,1,0+2\\} \\\\  & =\\{-1,0,1,2\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284713 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186284157 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284713 #edb/ref 1069 "q-174434" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284713 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284713 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}$, given that $I=\\{0,1,2\\},$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{0}=\\{0\\},\\,{S}_{1}=(0,1),\\,{S}_{2}=(0,2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284713 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "27878d76-ab4b-5705-b5cf-73536ef6aabb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284713 #edb/ref 1074 "The union of a family of indexed sets is the set containing all elements belonging to *at least one* set in the indexed family:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i} & ={S}_{0}\\cup {S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2} \\\\  & =\\{0\\}\\,\\cup \\,(0,1)\\,\\cup \\,(0,2) \\\\  & =[0,2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284714 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186284313 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284714 #edb/ref 1069 "q-174435" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284714 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284714 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}$, given that $I=\\{5,6,7\\},$ and\n${S}_{i}=[i,\\,i+1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284714 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8c85214a-dabe-59ba-93a3-34bf866976a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284714 #edb/ref 1074 "The union of a family of indexed sets is the set containing all elements belonging to *at least one* set in the indexed family:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i} & ={S}_{5}\\cup {S}_{6}\\cup {S}_{7} \\\\  & =[5,6)\\,\\cup \\,[6,7)\\,\\cup \\,[7,8) \\\\  & =[5,8).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284717 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186284037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284717 #edb/ref 1069 "q-174447" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284717 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284717 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $I=Z$ and ${X}_{i}=\\{i-1,\\,i\\},$ then ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284717 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f5b989ff-c36c-5cd1-a2e7-3a722d88ff08" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284717 #edb/ref 1074 "The intersection of a family of indexed sets $\\{{A}_{i}\\}_{i\\in I}$ contains all elements that belong to *all* sets in our family:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for all }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nLet's now write down a few instances of our indexed sets:\n\n- if $i=-1,$ we have ${X}_{-1}=\\{-2,-1\\}$\n\n- if $i=0,$ we have ${X}_{0}=\\{-1,0\\}$\n\n- if $i=1,$ we have ${X}_{1}=\\{0,1\\}$\n\nand so on. \n\nNotice that there is no element that belongs to all the sets. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284719 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186284197 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284719 #edb/ref 1069 "q-174450" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284719 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284719 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $I=N$ and ${X}_{i}=\\{-i,\\,0,\\,i\\},$ then ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284719 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2fd30642-b32d-59fc-bea9-4c1cd84ef2fd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186284719 #edb/ref 1074 "The union of a family of indexed sets is the set containing all elements belonging to *at least one* set in the indexed family:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nLet's now write down a few instances of our indexed sets:\n\n- if $i=1,$ we have ${X}_{1}=\\{-1,0,1\\}$\n\n- if $i=2,$ we have ${X}_{2}=\\{-2,0,2\\}$\n\n- if $i=3,$ we have ${X}_{3}=\\{-3,0,3\\}$\n\nand so on. \n\nNotice that all the integers belong to one of the sets.\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=Z.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301402 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186422742 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301402 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186422790 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301402 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186422852 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301402 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186422918 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301402 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186422924 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301402 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301402 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301402 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186422924 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186301402 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "371e7130-c050-59b2-8c27-7a7c79cf3390" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302397 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186301402 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302397 #edb/ref 1069 "q-32817" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302397 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302397 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/1f/1ffc0945ea74b1bd467a0b9935ee28b88be004c18b11492d67ecdfec56e1bb09.png)\n\nFind the parametric equations of the line shown in the figure above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302397 #edb/